<speak>Let me glance at the screen. Nothing needs an answer from me just now. The team is dealing with the supplier matter, and I should let them do that. This is one of the less obvious parts of stepping back: learning that seeing a conversation does not mean I need to join it. My assistant has been very tactful about it. She has started telling me when a message is simply for visibility, which is helpful without making a ceremony of the change.</speak>